1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:06,890
Meet Cedar and Sage, a small caterer in Cape Town
preparing its first corporate lunch quote.

2
00:00:06,890 --> 00:00:10,642
Alex, the operations manager, has a new CateringMS
workspace.

3
00:00:10,642 --> 00:00:20,231
Follow along as Alex sets up the company information,
chooses how customers will pay, and gets the team ready
for that first quote.

4
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:29,777
On the Business screen, Alex checks the business name and
contact email, then enters Cedar and Sage Catering as the
trading name.

5
00:00:29,777 --> 00:00:36,025
These details appear on customer documents and emails, so
use the inbox your team regularly checks.

6
00:00:36,025 --> 00:00:37,587
Select Save and continue.

7
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:44,489
For our corporate lunch, the driver leaves from Cedar and
Sage's kitchen in Cape Town.

8
00:00:44,489 --> 00:00:48,867
Alex enters that kitchen address here, rather than the
client's venue.

9
00:00:48,867 --> 00:00:54,836
CateringMS uses the dispatch address as the starting point
for delivery distances and route planning.

10
00:00:55,787 --> 00:00:58,922
Cedar and Sage uses forest green and copper.

11
00:00:58,922 --> 00:01:04,017
Alex enters those as the primary and secondary colours and
checks the preview.

12
00:01:04,017 --> 00:01:08,328
If your logo is hosted online, add its direct image link.

13
00:01:08,328 --> 00:01:12,639
This branding carries through to the customer portal and
customer documents.

14
00:01:13,587 --> 00:01:16,404
The corporate client may prefer a bank transfer.

15
00:01:16,404 --> 00:01:22,040
If Cedar and Sage wants to offer that option, Alex adds
the company's banking details here.

16
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:28,380
When a client selects EFT, they see where to pay and use
the invoice number as the reference.

17
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:31,197
Leave this blank if you don't accept transfers.

18
00:01:32,153 --> 00:01:35,061
A different client may want to pay online.

19
00:01:35,061 --> 00:01:39,422
Alex can connect Cedar and Sage's own payment provider on
this screen.

20
00:01:39,422 --> 00:01:43,056
If the provider account isn't ready, select Skip for now.

21
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:47,416
The company can return to payment settings when the
account is ready.

22
00:01:48,353 --> 00:01:54,667
For this example, Cedar and Sage isn't registered for VAT,
so Alex leaves the switch off.

23
00:01:54,667 --> 00:01:59,797
If your company is registered, turn it on and enter the
registration number.

24
00:01:59,797 --> 00:02:03,743
CateringMS uses this setting to choose the appropriate
invoice heading.

25
00:02:04,687 --> 00:02:10,710
Cedar and Sage hasn't verified its own email domain yet,
so Alex chooses the shared CateringMS sender.

26
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:13,544
Clients can reply to the company's contact email.

27
00:02:13,544 --> 00:02:20,276
If you want quotes to come from your own domain, you can
set it up and verify it later.

28
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:25,712
Alex wants to know when a client takes action on a quote.

29
00:02:25,712 --> 00:02:29,829
Review the alert preferences and choose the events your
team needs.

30
00:02:29,829 --> 00:02:34,320
Then enable push notifications on the phone or tablet you
actually use.

31
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,315
Each device needs to be set up separately.

32
00:02:38,253 --> 00:02:44,366
For the corporate lunch, suppose Cedar and Sage requires
payment seven days before the event.

33
00:02:44,366 --> 00:02:48,033
Alex would enter seven and choose Before the event.

34
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:54,960
To send a reminder two days before payment is due, select
the reminder option and enter two.

35
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,590
Review automatic emails separately.

36
00:02:57,553 --> 00:03:01,199
Cedar and Sage already has a spreadsheet of corporate
contacts.

37
00:03:01,199 --> 00:03:08,490
Alex can upload it as Excel or C S V, then review how the
columns match before confirming the import.

38
00:03:08,490 --> 00:03:11,771
Each client needs a name and an email address.

39
00:03:11,771 --> 00:03:15,416
If you're starting with an empty list, skip this step.

40
00:03:16,353 --> 00:03:21,984
Alex checks the setup summary, then selects Finish setup
and go to dashboard.

41
00:03:21,984 --> 00:03:26,749
Cedar and Sage can return to settings as its needs change.

42
00:03:26,749 --> 00:03:33,680
For example, it can connect WhatsApp later if the team
wants to manage customer replies there.

43
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:38,636
The dashboard shows what Cedar and Sage needs to do next.

44
00:03:38,636 --> 00:03:43,381
Alex can invite the team, then add the corporate lunch
menu and prices.

45
00:03:43,381 --> 00:03:51,778
When you're setting up your own workspace, open this
checklist and start with the next task you need to prepare
your first quote.
